# Support Guide catalog

When you add a **sidebar menu**, **route**, or **user-facing function** (button, modal, workflow), register it so Support Guide search can find it.

## Menus

Add the item to `SIDEBAR_MENU` in `src/lib/appCatalog.ts`. The Support Guide picks it up automatically. Then render it from that catalog in `Sidebar.tsx`.

## Extra pages (not in the sidebar)

Add to `EXTRA_APP_PAGES` in `src/lib/appCatalog.ts`.

## Form fields and checkboxes (Add Patient Email Notifications, etc.)

Add to `APP_FORM_FIELDS` in `src/lib/appCatalog.ts` (or use `addPatientField`-style helpers). Include the exact on-screen label so Support Guide search finds it.

## In-page functions (Add Patient, Export, Book, etc.)

Add to `APP_FUNCTIONS` in `src/lib/appCatalog.ts`, including:

- `name` people would search (include synonyms)
- `keywords` such as "new patient registration", "add patient"
- `path` to open with **Go there**
- `usedFor` and `steps`

Or call `registerSupportGuide()` from `src/lib/supportGuide.ts` when a feature module loads.

Do not leave a new screen or primary button undocumented.
